RAPP OS 1.0 "Doghouse"

You are looking at a real file. It is not embedded in the page and it is not
faked by the shell. It is served from:

    https://kody-w.github.io/OS/system32/etc/motd

curl it from your terminal right now and you will get these exact bytes. That
is the whole idea of the DOG layer: the global filesystem is addressed by real
URLs, so anything that speaks HTTP can read it -- this shell, your terminal,
another agent, a script you write in ten years.

The GOD layer is the opposite. It lives in IndexedDB on the single device you
are sitting at, it is writable, and nobody else can reach it, including me.

    ls /god          what is yours
    ls /OS/system32  what is everyone's
    stat <path>      which layer a path actually came from
